            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbative quantum field theory
            %em educated guess
            – jargon:
            %em trial wavefunction
            – as to what the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+states"} ground states
            of these systems should approximately look like to some approximation — a guess that turns out to agree accurately with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Mikhailov24"} Mikhailov 2024
          %h3#BasicLaughlinWavefunctionOnThePlane Basic Laughlin wavefunction on the plane
          %p
            The basic Laughlin wavefunction &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Laughlin83"}> Laughlin 1983 (6-7)
            , cf.
            = succeed "&rbrack;," do
              %a{:href => "#Laughlin99"} Laughlin 1999 (21)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            spin-less (in practice really:
            %em spin-polarized
            by a strong transversal
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"}> electrons
            , constrained to move) in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/odd+number"} odd
            “
            %em> Landau level filling fraction
            ”
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q  \,\in\, 2\mathbb{N} + 1
                  \\,,
          %p
            is the
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space+of+points"}
              configuration space of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              ordered points
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/plane"} plane
            — to be thought of as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+plane"} complex plane
            with canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+function"} holomorphic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+function"} coordinate function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z
            —, given (up to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalization"} normalization
          #eq:BasicLaughlinState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi La
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℓ
                            %mi B
                            %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
                      %msup
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %msub
                            %mi z
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi_{La}\big(
                  z_1, \cdots, z_N
                  \\big)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\textstyle{\prod_{i \lt j}}
                  (z_i - z_j)^q
                  \\;
                  \\exp\big(
                  \-
                  \\tfrac{1}{4 \ell_B^2}
                  \\textstyle{\sum_i} {\vert z_i\vert}^2
                  \\big)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/absolute+value"} absolute value
            of and hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+density"} probability density
            encoded by
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %strong second factor
                drops quickly where the particles are farther away from their center of mass (here: the origin in the complex plane) than the
                %em magnetic length
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mi B
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ≔
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msqrt
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %mi ℏ
                            %mi c
                          %mrow
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi e
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\ell_B \,\coloneqq\,
                      \\sqrt{
                      \\frac
                      { \hbar c }
                      { {\vert e \vert} B }
                      }
              %p
                (where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
                denotes the given external
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
                while the other constants are
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+units"} physical units
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
                is
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/speed+of+light"} speed of light
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+charge"} electric charge
                of an
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            %li
              %p
                while that of the
                %strong first factor
                tends to zero wherever any pair of particles approaches each other.
          %p
            Hence the particles in this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+state"} quantum state
            are most likely to be found all close to the origin but still spread out not to be too close to each other: The image is that of a little
            = succeed "," do
              %em droplet
            %em quantum fluid droplets
            in this context.
          %p
            Moreover, if or since the first factor (the
            = succeed ")" do
              %em Jastrow polynomial
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vandermonde+determinant"} Vandermonde determinant
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi vd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
