                  vd(z_\bullet)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\textstyle{\underset{i \lt j}{\prod}}
                  (z_i - z_j)
                  \\,,
          %p
            which itself is skew-symmetric under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
            of the particle positions (see
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "Vandermonde+determinant#SkewSymemtryUnderSwappingVariables"} there
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+many+body+physics"} many-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pauli+exclusion+principle"} Pauli exclusion principle
          %p
            Due to these basic properties, the Laughlin wavefunction is a plausible Ansatz for any localized
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            to which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vandermonde+determinant"} Vandermonde determinant
            is taken makes these particles support “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            \-fractional” quasi-particle/hole excitations, see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#BasicLaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles"} below
          %h3#MooreReadWavefunctionOnPlane Basic Moore-Read wavefunction on the plane
          %p
