            filling fraction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ∈
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  q  \,\in\, 2 \mathbb{N}
                  \\,,
          %p
            the Laughlin Ansatz needs modification, since here the even power of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vandermonde+determinant"} Vandermonde determinant
            would be symmetric under particle exchange and hence not describe the intended
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fermions"} Fermions
          %p
            A further educated guess suggests to multiply, at even filling fraction, the Laughlin wavefunction by some other factor which
            %em is
            skew-symmetric in the particle positions. The
            %em Moore-Read wavefunction
            \&amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#MooreRead91"}> Moore &amp; Read 1991 (5.1)
            \&amp;rbrack; is the result of choosing this factor to be the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian"} Pfaffian
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi pf
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pf(-)
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            of inverse
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distances"} distances
            between pairs of particles
          %blockquote
            %p
              (For the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pfaffian"} Pfaffian
              to be defined in this situation, we must consider an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              of electrons. But in the practice of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+effect"} fractional quantum Hall effect
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a humongous “macroscopic” number on the scale of the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Avogadro+constant"} Avogadro constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
              without any conceivable restriction of practical generality.)
          %p
            – whence often known as
            = succeed ":" do
              %em the Pfaffian state
          #eq:BasicMooreReadState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi MR
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi pf
                  %mrow
                    %mo (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mn 1
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mi z
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mo •
                                %mn 2
                    %mo )
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi j
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi q
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %msubsup
                            %mi ℓ
                            %mi B
                            %mn 2
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mi i
