                %ol
                  %li
                    %p
                      the ordinary
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Laughlin+state"} Laughlin state
                      is
                      %em skew-symmetric
                      in its arguments — as befits the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
                      of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+many-body+physics"} multiple
                      = succeed "," do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermions"} fermions
                  %li
                    %p
                      the Pfaffian Moore-Read state is
                      %em symmetric
                      in its arguments — as befits the
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
                      of
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+many-body+physics"} multiple
                      = succeed "." do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
              %li
                %p
                  for even filling fraction
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
                  it is the other way around.
            %p
