              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#PuBalramFremlingGromovPapić23"} Pu, Balram, Fremling, Gromov &amp; Papić 2023
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "#LiuZhaoXiang24"} Liu, Zhao &amp; Xiang 2024
          %h3#BasicLaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles Basic Laughlin wavefunction with quasi-holes
          %p
            The above Laughlin- and Moore-Read-wavefunctions are meant to model the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+states"} ground states
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fractional+quantum+Hall+systems"} fractional quantum Hall systems
            at
            %em exact
            Landau level-filling fraction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ν
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nu = 1/q
            where, so the idea, every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            forms a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound state
            with exactly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quanta"} quanta
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+flux"} magnetic flux
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "quantum+Hall+effect#IdeaFQHE"} there
          %p
            But if then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
            is increased by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            units of flux, a net total of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            flux quanta must remain un-paired with electrons. Still imagining that also these un-paired flux quanta are localized in the quantum Hall material, reflected in little
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortices"} vortices
            in the “electron fluid”, they are imagined to correspond to “holes” (jargon “quasi-holes”) in the electron fluid: points where electrons are forced to be
            = succeed "." do
              %em absent
          %p
            A now common proposal for how to modify the basic Laughlin state
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BasicLaughlinState"} (1)
            to reflect the presence of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            such quasi-holes at positions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a \in \mathbb{C}
            is to mak these be the external parameters for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
            of the form &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#Laughlin83"}> Laughlin 1983 (13)
            \&amp;rbrack;
          #eq:LaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles.maruku-equation
