                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{ccl}
                  \\psi
                  ^{(\xi_1, \cdots, \xi_n)}
                  _{La}(z_1, \cdots, z_N)
                  \&amp;\coloneqq&amp;
                  \\textstyle{\prod_a} \prod_{i} (z_i - \xi_a)
                  \\,
                  \\psi_{La}(z_1, \cdots, z_N)
                  \\\
                  \&amp;=&amp;
                  \\textstyle{\prod_a} \prod_{i} (z_i - \xi_a)
                  \\,
                  \\textstyle{\prod_{i \lt j}}
                  (z_i - z_j)^q
                  \\;
                  \\exp\big(
                  \-
                  \\tfrac{1}{4 \ell_B^2}
                  \\textstyle{\sum_i} {\vert z_i\vert}^2
                  \\big)
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            Clearly, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+density"} probability density
            of this wavefunction vanishes whenever at least one of the electron positions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_i
            coincides with one of the “electron hole” positions
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/angular+momentum"} angular momentum
            concentrated around these holes, as expected for electon-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vortices"} vortices
            centered at the
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a
          %p
            Beware that these holes at positions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a
            are not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
            like the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            at positions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} z_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_i
            are
            = succeed ":" do
              %em external parameters
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            of the fractional quantum Hall system parameterized by hole positions, and the above wavefunction
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles"} (5)
            would be an approximation to its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
          %p
            As such, the hole positions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a
            are “not dynamical” as the electrons are, but may, at least in principle, be moved by forces from outside the system, by changing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hamiltonian"} Hamiltonian
            across its parameter space. Such an
            %em external parameter-movement
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum system
            is described by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} quantum adiabatic theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ξ
                    %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a
            around another will return the quantum state
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles"} (5)
            to itself up to (an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Aharonov-Bohm+effect"} Aharonov-Bohm effect
            due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/magnetic+field"} magnetic field
            and) a
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phase"} Berry phase
            = succeed "&rbrack;" do
              %a{:href => "#ArovasSchriefferWilczek84"} Arovas, Schrieffer &amp; Wilczek 1984 (12)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi e
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi q
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  e^{
                  2 \pi \mathrm{i} / q
                  }
                  \\,,
          %p
            which means that away from the case of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integer+quantum+Hall+effect"} integer quantum Hall effect
            where
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q = 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+state"} ground state
            wavefunction will
            %em not quite return to itself
            as its defect positions are rotated around each other, but only up to a phase.
          %p
            Such fractional
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phases"} Berry phases
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} defects
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            movement are said to identify the defects as being (abelian)
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anyons"} anyons
          %p
            Beware that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berry+phases"} Berry phases
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} defect
            parameters are conceptually different from “quantum statistics” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
            (even if most expositions will say otherwise, and even if the very term “anyon” suggests otherwise): For one, the wavefunction
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LaughlinStateWithQuasiHoles"} (5)
            is
            %em symmetric
            in the hole positions which, if these were positions of dynamical particles, would make them
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosons"} bosons
          %p
            In particular, some of the quasi-hole positions may as well coincide,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a = \xi_b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            %em coincident
            quasi-holes (at some position
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ξ
                      %mi a
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi ξ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi_a \coloneqq \xi \in \mathbb{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            electrons equals the Laughlin wavefunction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N + 1
            electrons with one held fixed at
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ξ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \xi
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi La
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ξ
                        %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi ξ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi La
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ξ
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi z
                    %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\psi_{La}^{(\xi_1 = \xi, \cdots, \xi_q = \xi)}(
                  z_1, \cdots, z_N)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\psi_{La}(
                  \\xi, z_1, \cdots, z_N
                  )
          %p
            gives another view of how the quasi-holes are
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              \-fractional
            objects as compared to the electrons.
          %h3#GMPExcitationsOfLaughlinStates GMP-excitations of Laughlin states
          %p
            There is supposed to be a “density wave” excitation of quantum Hall ground states — called the “magneto-roton” &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GirvinMacDonaldPlatzman86"}> Girvin, MacDonald &amp; Platzman 1986
            \&amp;rbrack; —, which, for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavevector"} wavevector
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavefunction"} wavefunction
            modeled by acting with the “LLL-projected density operator” (
            %a{:href => "#GirvinMacDonaldPlatzman86"}> GMP86 (4.8)
            , reviewed by
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"} Gromov, Martinec &amp; Ryu 2020 (1-8)
          #eq:DensityOperator.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo ¯
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{\rho}_k
                  \\,\coloneqq\,
                  \\textstyle{\sum_i}
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \mathrm{i} \overline{k} \partial_i
                  \\big)
                  \\,
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \tfrac{\mathrm{i}}{2} \overline{k} z^i
                  \\big)
          %p
            on the given Laughlin/Moore-Read ground state, for instance the GMP-excitation of a Moore-Read state
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BasicMooreReadState"} (2)
            is described by the wavefunction
          #eq:GMPExcitationOfMRState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (7)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mrow
                      %mi GMP
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi MR
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi_{GMP,k}
                  \\,\coloneqq\,
                  \\overline{\rho}_{k} \, \Psi_{MR}
                  \\,.
          %p
            In fact, for the Moore-Read state another, second, excitation is expected &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GreiterWenWilczek91"}> Greiter, Wen &amp; Wilczek 1991
            \&amp;rbrack;, a “neutral fermion” excitation with putative wavefunction to be denoted
          #eq:GWWExcitationOfMRState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (8)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mrow
                      %mi NF
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi_{NF, k}
                  \\,.
          %p
            However &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"}> Gromov, Martinec &amp; Ryu 2020
            \&amp;rbrack;, a “simple and intuitive construction” of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mrow
                      %mi NF
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi_{NF,k}
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GWWExcitationOfMRState"} (8)
            similar to
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GMPExcitationOfMRState"} (7)
            “has been lacking”, but is provided by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            formulation
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#SupersymmetryBetweenLaughlinAndMooreReadStates"} above
          %p
            First, the density operator
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:DensityOperator"} (6)
            is the bosonic part of the following “LLL-projected
            = succeed "-density" do
              %em super
            = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
              %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"} GMR20 (19)
          #eq:SuperDensityOperator.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (9)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ¯
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi κ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mi i
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo ¯
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi k
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mi z
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %mn 2
                    %mi κ
                    %msup
                      %mi θ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %mfrac
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                        %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mi κ
                      %mo ¯
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi θ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\overline{\rho}_{k, \kappa}
                  \\,\coloneqq\,
                  \\textstyle{\sum_i}
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \mathrm{i} \overline{k} \partial_i
                  \\big)
                  \\,
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \tfrac{\mathrm{i}}{2} \overline{k} z^i
                  \\big)
                  \\,
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \tfrac{\mathrm{i}}{2} \kappa \theta^i
                  \\big)
                  \\,
                  \\exp\big(
                  \- \tfrac{\mathrm{i}}{2} \overline{\kappa} \overline{\theta}^i
                  \\big)
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi κ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            is the odd component of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super-
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wavevector"} wavevector
          %p
            Acting with this on the super-Laughlin wavefunction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mi sLa
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi_{sLa}
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BasciSuperLaughlinWavefunction"} (3)
            and projecting on the top super-component, as appropriate
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MRStateAsTopSuperstateComponent"} (4)
            for the Moore-Read state &amp;lbrack;
            %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"}> GMR20 (24)
            \&amp;rbrack;
          #eq:SuperGMPState.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (10)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ψ
                    %mrow
                      %mi MR
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %mi κ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mo ∫
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi i
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} d
                      %msup
                        %mi θ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi κ
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi sLa
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Psi_{MR, (k,\kappa)}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\textstyle{\int}
                  \\big(
                  \\textstyle{\prod}_i \mathrm{d}\theta^i
                  \\big)
                  \\,
                  \\overline{\rho}_{k, \kappa}
                  \\Psi_{sLa}
          %p
            describes indeed two different excitations of the Moore-Read state, depending on the parity of the number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electrons"} electrons
            in the system:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
                (as it must be for the plain MR state) then
              %p
                since
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi sLa
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi_{sLa}
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:BasciSuperLaughlinWavefunction"} (3)
                manifestly has vanishing coefficients for odd
                = succeed "-powers," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
                = succeed "-powers" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi θ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{\rho}_{k, \kappa}
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperDensityOperator"} (9)
                contribute to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Berezinian+integral"} Berezinian integral
                in
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperGMPState"} (10)
                = succeed "&rbrack;:" do
                  %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"} GMR20 (25)
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                      %mo ∈
                      %mn 2
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ⇒
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mrow
                          %mi MR
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi k
                          %mo ,
                          %mi κ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo =
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi ρ
                          %mo ¯
                        %mi k
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi MR
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      N \in 2\mathbb{N}
                      \\;\;\;\;\;
                      \\Rightarrow
                      \\;\;\;\;\;
                      \\Psi_{MR, (k,\kappa)}
                      \\;=\;
                      \\overline{\rho}_{k}
                      \\,
                      \\Psi_{MR}
            %li
              %p
                %strong
                  If
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
                  is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
                (such as after adding one electron to the MR state) then
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SuperGMPState"} (10)
                is of the form &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "#GromovMartinecRyu20"}> GMR20 (26)
                \&amp;rbrack;
              .maruku-equation
